                "quoted_status_profile_id": "114756202",
                "quoted_status_profile_username": "HouseCommerce",
                "reply_count": 26,
                "retweet_count": 28,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Here is an example of how the provider tax scams work:\n\nIn a state, hospitals could agree to pay $10 million in provider taxes, and the state would increase Medicaid payments to hospitals by $20 million \n\n(not necessarily improving any benefits for the recipients - recently in IN $2.6B of Medicaid dollars were diverted by hospitals from the seniors in nursing homes).\n\nAssuming the state had a 75% FMAP, the state would then receive $15 million in federal Medicaid matching funds (75% of $20 million).\n\nAs a result:\n\n- hospitals would gain $10 million ($20 million in increased Medicaid payments minus $10 million in tax payments), \n\n- the state would gain $5 million ($25 million from the hospitals and the federal government minus the $20 million paid to the hospitals), \n\nand the federal government would pay  $15 million.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
